// Runs the complete permanent deletion lifecycle for one account. The durable
// command closes these steps in order: Kratos termination, removal of every
// SpiceDB relation for the account_identity subject, account_identity anchor
// deletion, then either Member tombstone and audit preservation (TOMBSTONE) or
// removal of the pre-onboarding Member and its account anchor
// (UNONBOARDED_HARD_DELETE). Only TOMBSTONE sends completion mail.
// The bounded snapshot carries the exact notification/avatar inputs required
// after Identity deletion; PGMQ owns visibility retries, archival, and
// intentional replay. Avatar retirement remains an independent idempotent
// command and may be retried separately. A command with mode
// UNSPECIFIED is malformed and must be rejected;
// consumers must not infer TOMBSTONE or UNONBOARDED_HARD_DELETE from it.
